  "id": "COMPOUND:41722 - PROTEIN:6336",
  "verbalization": "Notoamide I is shown to interact with HL-60 cells, a human promyelocytic leukemia cell line, and its target is Thrombopoietin. This relationship is supported by multiple pathways, all of which lead through HL-60 to Thrombopoietin. The mechanism involves Notoamide I inhibiting the activity of HL-60 cells, which in turn affects Thrombopoietin. The evidence suggests that Notoamide I may act as a modulator of the signaling pathways that regulate Thrombopoietin expression, potentially through the suppression of certain cellular processes in HL-60. The presence of multiple targets in the HL-60 cell line, including Vestitone and 1,2-Di(Propan-2-Yl)Benzene, further supports the notion that Notoamide I influences a broader network of cellular responses, which could ultimately impact Thrombopoietin production. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Notoamide I to exert a regulatory effect on Thrombopoietin through a complex, multi-step mechanism involving cellular targets.",
